---
import Arrow from '../../components/Arrow.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Artificial Intelligence — Conscia Labs"
  description="Conscia Labs studies agentic systems, AI protocols, and the security controls that make them workable in an organization."
  noIndex
>
  <div class="focus-detail-shell">
    <Header />
    <section class="focus-detail-hero" aria-labelledby="focus-detail-title">
      <div class="container">
        <a class="back-link" href="/#focus-areas"><Arrow /> All focus areas</a>
        <div class="focus-detail-hero__grid">
          <div class="focus-detail-hero__copy">
            <p class="project-detail-meta">01 <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Focus area</p>
            <h1 id="focus-detail-title">Artificial Intelligence</h1>
            <p class="focus-detail-hero__lede">Systems that can act, collaborate, and stay within clear boundaries.</p>
            <p class="focus-detail-hero__description">We are looking closely at agentic systems: how they reason, use tools, work with other agents, and operate over time. The design challenge is making that work useful while keeping authority and limits visible to the organization.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="agentic-map" aria-label="A conceptual map of an agentic system">
            <div class="agentic-map__orbit agentic-map__orbit--outer"></div>
            <div class="agentic-map__orbit agentic-map__orbit--inner"></div>
            <div class="agentic-map__connection agentic-map__connection--one"></div>
            <div class="agentic-map__connection agentic-map__connection--two"></div>
            <div class="agentic-map__connection agentic-map__connection--three"></div>
            <span class="agentic-map__node agentic-map__node--agent">AGENT</span>
            <span class="agentic-map__node agentic-map__node--protocol">A2A</span>
            <span class="agentic-map__node agentic-map__node--security">SECURITY</span>
            <span class="agentic-map__node agentic-map__node--context">CONTEXT</span>
            <span class="agentic-map__boundary">ENTERPRISE BOUNDARY</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="focus-detail-overview section-light" aria-labelledby="focus-question-title">
      <div class="container focus-detail-overview__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">01 / The challenge</p>
          <h2 id="focus-question-title">Useful autonomy needs a clear boundary.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="focus-detail-overview__copy">
          <p>An agent can plan a task, call tools, coordinate steps, and hand work to another system. Once it does that, authority, identity, data, and accountability become part of the design.</p>
          <p>We turn those concerns into patterns an organization can use: systems with enough autonomy to help, clear limits on what they can do, and a record of the decisions they make.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="focus-detail-threads section-dark" aria-labelledby="threads-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro section-intro--dark">
          <div>
            <p class="section-label">02 / Current threads</p>
            <h2 id="threads-title">The system around an agent.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>We study the full system around an agent’s action: the agent, the protocols it uses, and the controls that keep its work within the right scope.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="focus-detail-thread-grid">
          <article class="focus-detail-thread" style="--item-accent: var(--accent-bright)">
            <span class="focus-detail-thread__number">01</span>
            <h3>Agentic systems</h3>
            <p>We test how agents plan, keep context, use tools, recover from errors, and coordinate over longer tasks.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="focus-detail-thread" style="--item-accent: var(--accent-info)">
            <span class="focus-detail-thread__number">02</span>
            <h3>Protocols and coordination</h3>
            <p>We study protocols such as A2A and initiatives such as Agntcy, with a focus on discovery, communication, delegation, and clear responsibility.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="focus-detail-thread" style="--item-accent: var(--accent-secondary)">
            <span class="focus-detail-thread__number">03</span>
            <h3>Enterprise security</h3>
            <p>We work through identity, permissions, policy, audit trails, and safe tool access for agents inside an organization.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="focus-detail-boundaries section-light" aria-labelledby="boundaries-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro section-intro--light">
          <div>
            <p class="section-label">03 / Guardrails</p>
            <h2 id="boundaries-title">An agent needs a defined scope.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>The hard part is giving an agent enough room to help while keeping its authority clear.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="boundary-grid">
          <article class="boundary-card">
            <span class="boundary-card__marker">DEFINE</span>
            <h3>Make authority explicit.</h3>
            <p>Tie the agent to a person, team, service, or approved workflow so its authority is clear.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="boundary-card">
            <span class="boundary-card__marker">OBSERVE</span>
            <h3>Keep a record.</h3>
            <p>Keep decisions, tool calls, handoffs, and outcomes visible enough to review and learn from.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="boundary-card">
            <span class="boundary-card__marker">CONTAIN</span>
            <h3>Set the limit.</h3>
            <p>Set clear limits for data, tools, scope, and escalation when conditions change.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="focus-detail-practice section-dark" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
      <div class="container focus-detail-practice__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">04 / How we work</p>
          <h2 id="practice-title">We take ideas into real systems.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="focus-detail-practice__steps">
          <div class="practice-step">
            <span>01</span>
            <p><strong>Study</strong> the capabilities, protocols, and failure modes that shape agentic systems.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="practice-step">
            <span>02</span>
            <p><strong>Test</strong> ideas against the practical realities of enterprise security, governance, and operations.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="practice-step">
            <span>03</span>
            <p><strong>Build</strong> patterns into prototypes, guidance, and products people can use.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="focus-detail-cta section-dark" aria-labelledby="ai-cta-title">
      <div class="container focus-detail-cta__inner">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Related project</p>
          <h2 id="ai-cta-title">A governed route to enterprise AI.</h2>
          <p>AI Gateway puts these ideas into a product: a secure, multi-tenant route to model access for organizations. It is currently in closed beta.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button button--outline" href="/projects/ai-gateway">Explore AI Gateway <Arrow /></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Footer />
  </div>
</Layout>
